  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1230 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge, currently centered over the Four Corners\nregion, will broaden east this weekend. As a result, above\naverage temperatures return to the Mid-South with highs reaching\nthe mid to upper 90s by Sunday. Unfortunately, hot conditions\nwill persist into next week as the ridge centers over the mid\nMississippi Valley. The LREF continues to place low probabilities\n(less than 10 percent) of heat indices reaching 105 degrees on\nMonday and Tuesday. This is due to a lack of appreciable moisture\nreturning into the Mid-South, keeping dewpoints on the lower end.\n\nBy midweek, both the GFS and ECMWF depict a weak upper level low\nslowly retrograding across middle Mississippi. This system will\nbring increased moisture to the Mid-South along with a low chance\nfor isolated showers Wednesday into Thursday. Should any\nprecipitation occur, amounts will be negligible. The greater\nimpact brought by the upper low will be heat. Due to increased\ndewpoint temperatures, heat indices will approach and exceed\n105 degrees by the end of the week. A Heat Advisory will likely\nbe needed as early as Wednesday with the potential for Extreme\nHeat Warnings in the Mississippi Delta by the end of the week.\nUnfortunately, the long range outlook favors above normal\ntemperatures through the beginning of September. No sign of fall\njust yet.\n\nANS",
